# Cargo runs on a Composer 2.5 subagent

Do not run cargo in the parent shell, watch its log, or poll it.

`~/.bashrc` defines a `cargo` function. For `check`, `build`, `test`, `run`, `bench`, `fmt`, `clippy`, `fix`, `doc`, `rustc`, and `clean` (including `c`, `b`, `t`, `r`, and a leading `+toolchain`), it starts one background `agent --model composer-2.5` and returns the pid and log path under `~/.cache/cargo-dispatch/`. The agent runs that same command via `/usr/bin/cargo`. A `--release` command exports `CXXFLAGS="-include cstdint"`. `install` and `publish` are refused. Other subcommands, such as `metadata` and `tree`, call `/usr/bin/cargo` directly.

Shells that do not source `~/.bashrc` use the same split: one background Composer 2.5 agent, the exact command, no second cargo process.

One cargo process at a time. If cargo, rustc, or clippy is already running, do not start another. A workspace-wide check, test, or build only when the user explicitly says workspace. Native target is `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`. Do not install binaries or restart services from a cargo run.
